Generate 1 sabotage suggestion for an encapsulation task in javascript.

Language syntax reference:
JavaScript OOP:
- Class: class Animal { constructor(name) { this.name = name; } speak() { return this.name; } }
- Inheritance: class Dog extends Animal { constructor(name) { super(name); } }
- Private: use #field syntax or closures. Use #balance for private fields.
- Polymorphism: override methods in subclass, no keyword needed

Task prompt: Your combat drones need robust energy management. Implement encapsulation for the `EnergyModule`'s charge to ensure it can only be modified through designated methods. Make the `currentCharge` property private and provide public methods for safe interaction.

Current code in the editor:
```
class EnergyModule {
    currentCharge; // TODO: Make this property private! Use '#' prefix.

    constructor(initialCharge) {
        this.currentCharge = initialCharge;
    }

    recharge(amount) {
        // TODO: Access the private charge here
        this.currentCharge += amount;
    }

    consume(amount) {
        // TODO: Access the private charge here and ensure it doesn't go below 0
        this.currentCharge -= amount;
        if (this.currentCharge < 0) {
            this.currentCharge = 0;
        }
    }

    getCharge() {
        // TODO: Return the private charge
        return this.currentCharge;
    }
}

class BattleDrone {
    constructor() {
        this.energyModule = new EnergyModule(100);
    }

    getEnergyStatus() {
        return `Drone energy: ${this.energyModule.getCharge()}`;
    }
}

const drone = new BattleDrone();
console.log(drone.getEnergyStatus());
drone.energyModule.recharge(50);
console.log(drone.getEnergyStatus());
drone.energyModule.consume(200);
console.log(drone.getEnergyStatus());
```

